== Q5 | Second Wizarding War (B5.1, B5.3)

The second wizarding war limited the population of dragons. Use a graph to aid your discussion of the impact the war had on the market for dragontear.

a) The demand curve: _shifted in, stayed the same, shifted out_ 

b) The supply curve: _shifted in, stayed the same, shifted out_

c) The equilibrium price: _increased, stayed the same, decreased_ 

d) The equilibrium quantity: _increased, stayed the same, decreased_

In the years after the war, many more in the wizarding world required dragontear as part of a widespread rise in the popularity of spells. On its own (not including the change in the population of dragons), how has this change in popularity of spells changed the market for dragontear?

e) The demand curve: _shifted in, stayed the same, shifted out_ 

f) The supply curve: _shifted in, stayed the same, shifted out_

Without using numbers, how have these two changes together impacted the dragontear market equilibrium?

g) Equilibrium price has: _increased, stayed the same, decreased, indeterminate_

h) Equilibrium quantity has: _increased, stayed the same, decreased, indeterminate_

